# Pi hotpatch (Windows)

## Deploy path

- Target: `dsc@192.168.86.48`, container `dsc-hub-brain`, static at `/app/static/`.
- Use **PuTTY `plink` + `pscp`** with `-batch -hostkey` and `-pw` — OpenSSH `scp` hangs on password prompt in agent shells.

## Container lifecycle

- Prefer **`docker stop -t 20` + `start`** for brain reload after `docker cp`.
- Avoid **`docker restart`** (has hung this Pi) and **`docker kill`** (Pass 5 Task 5 hung the host; required operator power-cycle).
- If brain must reload mid-prove and Pi is healthy: stop+start only. For Zigbee MQTT inject / policy prove, use **resume scripts without kill** (see `.audit/live-ux-pass5-task5-zigbee-resume.ps1`).

## Prove flakes (not gate failures)

| Residual | Treat as |
|----------|----------|
| **Hold / Twin fleet lag** | After `POST /control/service`, `hass_extras` may stay stale **~1 poll (~5–10s)**. Wait/re-fetch `/fleet/computed` before asserting Hold off or Twin state — do not fail on first read. |
| **Twin fleet mirror vs command** | HTTP turn_on/brightness may succeed while fleet shows `off` without GPIO5 PWM — software accept path green; optical N/A. |
| **SF1000 / Twin Actual sub-0.1H** | Brief gate on/off cycles can show ~0.05H Actual while lamp OFF — rounding/stress artifact, not a live-ON lie. |
| **Historical `sf1000_on` gap** | No backfill — DutyStrip honesty improves **going forward** after hotpatch; do not chase retroactive history as a gate fix. |
| **`policy_state` after brain restart** | Clears until MQTT occupancy event — dry-pub re-seed in prove scripts before asserting Problem/Clear. |

